--- a/merger-brief.md
+++ b/merger-brief.md
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 
 **While a spec gate runs (`.claude/handoff/m1/push-hold` exists), the orchestrator starts no merger** (2026-10-26). If one exists when you start, stop at once and report "gate running": a merge's builds and tests beside the gate starve it.
 
+**While a red gate holds the milestone (`.claude/handoff/m1/red-hold` exists), merge only an item it lists as `fix <item>`** (owner, 2026-10-28): the next gate runs on the red head plus that red's fixes. For any other item, stop at once and report "held: gate red". `m1/run-merge.sh` refuses a gate whose range holds another merge.
+
 ## Steps
 
 1. `cd /Users/jb/Dev/goodfetch`. Check `git status` is clean and the branch is `milestone/m1-core`. Record the tip: `base=$(git rev-parse HEAD)`. `source .claude/handoff/m1/env.sh` in every Bash call that builds **or runs tests** (it sets `TMPDIR=/g`, so test folders stay off the RAM-backed /tmp; 2026-10-26).
